4. Feature Transformation

Categorical variables are transformed using One-Hot Encoding.

The preprocessing approach includes:

ColumnTransformer(
    transformers=[
        ("num", StandardScaler(), ["age", "bmi"]),
        ("cat", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore"),
         ["sex", "smoker", "region", "children"])
    ]
)

Numerical preprocessing

StandardScaler is used to standardize numerical variables.

Approximately:

mean = 0
standard deviation = 1

Categorical preprocessing

OneHotEncoder converts categorical values into numerical binary features.

For example:

region_northeast
region_northwest
region_southeast
region_southwest

handle_unknown="ignore" helps the API handle an unseen category without failing during transformation.

5. Machine Learning Pipeline

A Scikit-learn Pipeline and ColumnTransformer are used to keep preprocessing and model prediction consistent.

A simplified pipeline looks like:

Raw Input
   ↓
ColumnTransformer
   ↓
Numerical Scaling
   ↓
Categorical One-Hot Encoding
   ↓
Regression Model
   ↓
Predicted Charges

This prevents preprocessing logic from being duplicated between training and prediction.

6. Baseline Model — Linear Regression

Linear Regression was used as the baseline model.

Current baseline performance:

MAE          : 4214.91
RMSE         : 5810.03
R²           : 0.7826
Adjusted R²  : 0.7687

Interpretation

An R² of approximately 0.783 means the baseline model explains around 78.26% of the variance in medical charges on the evaluated test data.

The MAE of approximately $4,215 represents the average absolute difference between predicted and actual charges.

The RMSE of approximately $5,810 indicates that some larger prediction errors are present.

7. Final Model

The project uses an XGBoost regression model for the prediction API.

The trained model artifacts are stored in the model/ directory.

model/
├── best_model_xgboost.pkl
├── model_columns.pkl
├── model_metadata.pkl
├── predict.py
└── ...

The API loads the trained model and uses it to generate predictions from validated user input.

The exact final model metrics should be updated here when the final test evaluation is available.

