9. FastAPI Backend

The trained machine learning model is exposed through a REST API built using FastAPI.

The API is served using Uvicorn.

The application starts with:

uvicorn api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

API Documentation

After starting the application, open:

http://localhost:8000/docs

This opens the interactive Swagger UI, where you can inspect endpoints and send prediction requests.

Alternative documentation:

http://localhost:8000/redoc

10. Run Locally Without Docker

Step 1 — Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/Arvind-rawat70/life-insurance-retention-prediction-api.git

Then:

cd insurance-api

Use the repository URL and folder name corresponding to your GitHub repository.

Step 2 — Create a virtual environment

Windows:

python -m venv .venv

Activate it:

.venv\Scripts\activate

Step 3 — Install dependencies

pip install -r req.txt

Step 4 — Start FastAPI

uvicorn api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

Then open:

http://localhost:8000/docs

🐳 Docker

Docker is used to package the application together with its Python runtime and dependencies.

This makes the application easier to run consistently across different environments.

Dockerfile

FROM python:3.11

WORKDIR /app

COPY req.txt .

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r req.txt

COPY . .

EXPOSE 8000

CMD ["uvicorn", "api:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000"]

What the Dockerfile does

Instruction

Purpose

FROM python:3.11

Uses Python 3.11

WORKDIR /app

Sets /app as the working directory

COPY req.txt .

Copies dependency file

RUN pip install ...

Installs Python packages

COPY . .

Copies application files

EXPOSE 8000

Documents application port

CMD ...

Starts FastAPI

11. Build the Docker Image

Make sure Docker Desktop is running.

From the project directory:

docker build -t arvind886/insurance_premium-api:latest .

Check the image:

docker images

Expected repository:

arvind886/insurance_premium-api

12. Run the Docker Container

docker run -p 8000:8000 arvind886/insurance_premium-api:latest

The mapping is:

8000:8000
  ↑     ↑
host  container

The FastAPI application will then be available at:

http://localhost:8000

Swagger UI:

http://localhost:8000/docs

13. Docker Hub

The Docker image is published under:

