15. Model Evaluation

The project evaluates regression models using:

MAE — Mean Absolute Error

Lower = Better

MAE measures the average absolute difference between actual and predicted charges.

RMSE — Root Mean Squared Error

Lower = Better

RMSE penalizes larger prediction errors more strongly than MAE.

R² Score

Higher = Better

R² measures how much of the variation in the target is explained by the model.

Adjusted R²

Higher = Better

Adjusted R² accounts for the number of predictors in the model.

16. Model Comparison

The project initially evaluates Linear Regression and then compares it with tree-based regression algorithms.

Models considered include:

1. Linear Regression
2. Random Forest Regressor
3. Gradient Boosting Regressor
